course: dictionary
lesson: 13769
title: Life on the intertidal shore
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a place. «Intertidal» describes the strip of seashore that is under water at high tide and out in the air at low tide. Read the words around it for clues: sea, rocks, tide and seaweed all point to the shore.
explain: «The crab hid under a rock in the intertidal zone.» The rock and the tide tell you the crab lives on the shore, not in a field or a forest. Intertidal means between the high tide and low tide marks, so a rock pool that is covered at high tide and dry at low tide is intertidal.
explain: Animals and plants here must cope with two very different conditions. «Barnacles shut tight when the tide goes out and keep their water in.» They survive the dry times and the wet times, so they are tough. Always check: does your meaning still fit the sentence?
explain: Safety comes first. Tides can come back in fast, so check the tide times before you go exploring a rock pool.
fact: Intertidal means the part of the seashore between the high tide mark and the low tide mark.
fact: «The intertidal zone» is covered by the sea at high tide and is dry air at low tide.
fact: Intertidal plants and animals can survive both wet and dry times.
fact: Crabs, limpets, barnacles and seaweed are common intertidal creatures.
fact: Tides can come back in fast, so always check tide times before exploring the shore.
exercise: «The intertidal zone is covered by the sea at high tide.» What does intertidal mean? | A deep part of the ocean | *The strip of seashore between high and low tide | A sandy hill above the beach | A river that flows inland
exercise: Which of these is an intertidal creature? | *Barnacle | Eagle | Cactus | Camel
exercise: «Seaweed survives both wet and dry times in the intertidal zone.» Why must intertidal creatures be tough? | *They must cope with being under water and in the air | They never get wet | They live only in the deep sea | They fly between the rocks
test: «The tide comes in fast, so check tide times before you go.» Why should you check tide times? | To count the crabs | *To stay safe from the rising sea | To see how fast the sea is | To find the best sandwich shop
test: Which description fits the word intertidal best? | Deep trench under the ocean | *Strip of shore under water at high tide and in air at low tide | Mountain top covered in snow | Desert with sand dunes
exam: Mia says intertidal means a type of fish. Is she right? | Yes, a fish that lives in rivers | *No, it describes a strip of seashore that is wet at high tide and dry at low tide | No, it is a kind of cloud | Yes, a fish that lives in the deep ocean
